{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027564-turning-into-living-flame-how-to-do-this-in-second-edition","id":1027564,"title":"Turning into Living Flame: How to do this in second edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-06T05:52:18-08:00","id":1027564,"title":"Turning into Living Flame: How to do this in second edition?","content":"I distinctly remember their was an example Forces rote for this in 1st edition but don't have that book handy. IIRC it required Forces and Life. However 2nd edition Death has Shadow Flesh, a spell that allows the mage to turn into a sentient shadow, which doesnt require Life. Would you implement something similar for Forces 'Transmute self into energy' spells? It seems sensible to me, as the effect (while cool) doesnt feel like it should require a Double Adept to pull off. <br /> <br /> My real question is how would you handle this mechanically? I am not really sure where to begin. And then you get into the question of dealing with morphing into other things, like the Matter mage turning into stone or steel. Then your party Mastigos feels left out, so decides to try and turn himself into a sentient patch of Space! <br /> <br /> Advice and suggestions on how to deal with the mechanics of changing yourself into flame or other more exotic forms would be welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:03:19-08:00","id":1027573,"title":"","content":"Shadow Flesh has caused a lot of confusion. It should probably be Death 4 +Life 4, though maybe Dave will explain it if he ever gets the FAQ out. For now I'd assume that becoming living flame takes Forces 4 and Life 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T08:24:07-08:00","id":1027677,"title":"","content":"Yep, by the general rules of the system Shadow Flesh should be Death 4 + Life 4. Becoming living flame <i>should</i> be Forces 4 + Life 4 <i>buuuuut</i> the can of worms has been left open so if your group is ok with it then you might be able to get away with just Forces 4. Logically it's Shadow Flesh that needs to be changed, but if your group likes that you can turn yourself into a piece of your arcana at 4th dot rather than than it requiring you to be a second degree Adept then go ahead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T08:53:20-08:00","id":1027701,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, it does make more sense that it should require life as well. When I spotted Shadow Flesh my first thoughts were that the change was part of the general philosophy of removing some of the annoying speedbumps certain powers/arcana had in first edition. Things like Forces only being able to manipulate certain things at specific dot levels and the like. Last edition turning into a shadow would need Life, Death AND Matter if you didnt want to leave key things like clothes behind. But after going through the practices its hard to justify it not needing life. <br /> <br /> I don't have a Mage group at the moment, but if I get round to starting a game I will bring the issue up then.<br /> <br /> My other question was how would you deal with the mechanics of someone turning into flame? Assuming they had Forces and Life 4 that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T09:52:53-08:00","id":1027722,"title":"","content":"Turning into a living pillar of fire is explicitly called out in Creative Thaumaturgy as requiring both Forces and Life 4. Shadow Flesh is weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T09:58:33-08:00","id":1027725,"title":"","content":"Find a Changeling with Phantom Glory elemental seeming affinity and the Fairest affinity, and they can use the contract to turn you into living flames.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T11:11:31-08:00","id":1027762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027564-turning-into-living-flame-how-to-do-this-in-second-edition?p=1027725#post1027725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Find a Changeling with Phantom Glory elemental seeming affinity and the Fairest affinity, and they can use the contract to turn you into living flames.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the Mage forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T12:30:16-08:00","id":1027799,"title":"","content":"There may be a way to justify Shadow Flesh... Mage could go to Death Twilight kind of becoming his purview -&gt; change his new ghostly self into shadow -&gt; get out. The problem is that this level of complexity would require a Master to be cast as a single spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T12:42:47-08:00","id":1027805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027564-turning-into-living-flame-how-to-do-this-in-second-edition?p=1027762#post1027762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the Mage forum.</div> </div> </div> </div> So the Mage uses magic to mind control or bribe a Changeling who happens to be the Mages obsession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T13:09:04-08:00","id":1027817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027564-turning-into-living-flame-how-to-do-this-in-second-edition?p=1027805#post1027805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the Mage uses magic to mind control or bribe a Changeling who happens to be the Mages obsession.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a slightly more relevant answer, but only if we're talking about games that involve crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T15:34:18-08:00","id":1027875,"title":"","content":"To me Shadow Flesh should just be Death 4 because of how a shadow is on a metaphysical level. It's an end, an echo, so the spell Patterns you into that moment, preserved before dissolution, with all its benefits and drawbacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T15:51:47-08:00","id":1027884,"title":"","content":"You aren't ended yet, you're still a living Pattern and for purposes of your physical form fall under Life. So I still don't see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T15:58:16-08:00","id":1027889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027564-turning-into-living-flame-how-to-do-this-in-second-edition?p=1027884#post1027884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You aren't ended yet, you're still a living Pattern and for purposes of your physical form fall under Life. So I still don't see it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Doesn't matter what you are now, the spell only makes you what you will be. What all things end up being. Shadows and dust. That's the point. Life ends, Matter rots, Forces snuffed out. What remains? Death. <br /> <br /> Duh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T20:32:06-08:00","id":1028008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027564-turning-into-living-flame-how-to-do-this-in-second-edition?p=1027884#post1027884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You aren't ended yet, you're still a living Pattern and for purposes of your physical form fall under Life. So I still don't see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the same Arcanum that lets you put people in the same phase of existence as ghosts without killing them. Twilit Body does the same thing for Spirit. It's just possible that one of the two Arcana that cover ephemeral beings normally capable of materialization has an in with the symbolism connecting darkness and bodies with one of the five main components of the human soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T02:23:15-08:00","id":1028076,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think Death can sort of cheat a bit when it comes to affecting living beings.<br /> <br /> Think about it this way: <i>Any</i> arcarnum can be used to move things from Life's purview to Death's. Death itself is just better at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T13:37:53-08:00","id":1030227,"title":"","content":"The way I saw Death working with the shadow flesh spell, is kinda how I look at spirit. Everything has a shadow. Be it a rock, mouse or human. So the mage is simply enhancing the shadow aspect already present in the subject.<br /> <br /> With Spirit, humans don't have a spirit reflection and you can shift them to the twilight state or even across the Gauntlet without Life 4. The reason for this (as I have imagined); is that they do have a spirit, but it is directly bound to/contained within them. This is why you can shift a human into the Twilight state but objects are destroyed in the process.<br /> <br /> But I can see why people would want Life 4 to bring it in line with some of the other &quot;turn living matter into xxxxx&quot; spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T13:47:43-08:00","id":1030231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027564-turning-into-living-flame-how-to-do-this-in-second-edition?p=1030227#post1030227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I saw Death working with the shadow flesh spell, is kinda how I look at spirit. Everything has a shadow. Be it a rock, mouse or human. So the mage is simply enhancing the shadow aspect already present in the subject.<br /> <br /> With Spirit, humans don't have a spirit reflection and you can shift them to the twilight state or even across the Gauntlet without Life 4. The reason for this (as I have imagined); is that they do have a spirit, but it is directly bound to/contained within them. This is why you can shift a human into the Twilight state but objects are destroyed in the process.<br /> <br /> But I can see why people would want Life 4 to bring it in line with some of the other &quot;turn living matter into xxxxx&quot; spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, by that logic, can a mage turn into a living gravity well using only Forces 4? everything already exerts its own gravitational influence, so you could theoretically just enhance that already present aspect. Or what about a living force of luck using Fate, or a twisting mass of shifting Time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T14:18:26-08:00","id":1030245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027564-turning-into-living-flame-how-to-do-this-in-second-edition?p=1030231#post1030231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, by that logic, can a mage turn into a living gravity well using only Forces 4? everything already exerts its own gravitational influence, so you could theoretically just enhance that already present aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>A human has a soul, a shadow, and the capacity to die, decay, and/or manifest connections to the Underworld or its denizens. This is not comparable to erasing the line between flesh and flame. A human Forces Pattern does not have a total overlap with their Life Pattern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or what about a living force of luck using Fate, </div> </div> </div>Fate is a pervasive phenomenon attached to other discrete phenomena. Your Fate Pattern doesn't contain Forms analogous to a human body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or a twisting mass of shifting Time? </div> </div> </div>Temporal Stutter already exists if you just want to disappear into the linear procession of events in history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T14:51:37-08:00","id":1030263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027564-turning-into-living-flame-how-to-do-this-in-second-edition?p=1030245#post1030245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A human has a soul, a shadow, and the capacity to die, decay, and/or manifest connections to the Underworld or its denizens. This is not comparable to erasing the line between flesh and flame. A human Forces Pattern does not have a total overlap with their Life Pattern.<br /> <br /> Fate is a pervasive phenomenon attached to other discrete phenomena. Your Fate Pattern doesn't contain Forms analogous to a human body.<br /> <br /> Temporal Stutter already exists if you just want to disappear into the linear procession of events in history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadow also isn't the human body, and a human Shadow Pattern doesn't have total overlap with their Life pattern either. Hell, a human Death pattern doesn't have overlap unless we're talking undead. A normal human can't be controlled through Death while alive and can't be controlled through Life while dead. You can forcibly shove the power of Death into a living creature (Enervation and the like), sure, but you can do that with any arcana (A fireball would be equal to forced rot in this situation).<br /> <br /> I would argue that the gravitational field you exert is as much you as the shadow you cast. You can say that Shadow is a force unto itself, but by that regard so is Gravity. Each controllable by a different arcanum but that shouldn't really make a difference in this case. And if not luck, then Destiny should work just as well, because while luck itself might not be something you think belongs to an individual, their destiny most definitely is. It isn't just <i>a</i> Destiny, it is <i>your</i> Destiny.<br /> <br /> Lets be real, while you can <i>try</i> to justify its existence all you want, Shadow Flesh is an outlier that doesn't conform to normal Awakened magic rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T15:15:09-08:00","id":1030272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027564-turning-into-living-flame-how-to-do-this-in-second-edition?p=1030263#post1030263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadow also isn't the human body, and a human Shadow Pattern doesn't have total overlap with their Life pattern either.</div> </div> </div> </div>There <i>is </i>no &quot;Shadow Pattern.&quot; A human's shadow is part of their Death Pattern, as is their soul, the gradual breakdown of their body, and so on, but these are Forms, not entire Patterns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hell, a human Death pattern doesn't have overlap unless we're talking undead. </div> </div> </div><i>Memento mori</i> is an expression for a reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A normal human can't be controlled through Death while alive and can't be controlled through Life while dead. </div> </div> </div>A normal human can be made to be for-all-intents-and-purposes dead with a two-dot spell that has no need for the Life Arcanum, and the level of competency in this same Arcanum directly below Shadow Flesh allows you to Perfect the decay within a living subject to deal damage or turn shadows into solid objects. The level at which Shadow Flesh becomes available is also the level at which you become able to forcibly Materialize a ghost or override a human's will by causing them to be Possessed by a ghost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would argue that the gravitational field you exert is as much you as the shadow you cast. </div> </div> </div>Your gravitational field is not associated with an aspect of the human soul save through the same channels that Without A Trace and Empty Presence use \u2014 the metaphysical shadow is the impact a person has on the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if not luck, then Destiny should work just as well, because while luck itself might not be something you think belongs to an individual, their destiny most definitely is. It isn't just <i>a</i> Destiny, it is <i>your</i> Destiny. </div> </div> </div>Your Destiny is not a discrete object unattached to anything and the Forms it contains in your Fate Pattern cannot be reasonably drawn from any other Form in your Fate Pattern to cause your body to vanish.<br /> <br /> &quot;Luck doesn't belong to an individual&quot; is neither a thing I believe nor a thing that I said. You might as well claim that you can bless a specific patch of air or floor of a building without using Area Scale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lets be real, while you can <i>try</i> to justify its existence all you want, Shadow Flesh is an outlier that doesn't conform to normal Awakened magic rules. </div> </div> </div>Shadow Flesh is a spell in an Arcanum whose nigh-omnipresent purviews cannot be comprehensively summed up in one word, like most of the Subtle Arcana. The Gross Arcana correspond to definite manifest phenomena that can be pointed to as within or outside the bounds of one's influence \u2014 a bonfire is not a living thing, and its nonliving components are only partially energy from a symbolic perspective, but a mortal being has Death built into its very nomenclature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T15:17:40-08:00","id":1030275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027564-turning-into-living-flame-how-to-do-this-in-second-edition?p=1030272#post1030272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There <i>is </i>no &quot;Shadow Pattern.&quot; A human's shadow is part of their Death Pattern, as is their</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you not finish this on purpose or were you going to say Mind? I've been wondering if the human 'spirit' has been split among their ghost and Astral 'world' and presumably some others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T15:27:08-08:00","id":1030277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027564-turning-into-living-flame-how-to-do-this-in-second-edition?p=1030275#post1030275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you not finish this on purpose or were you going to say Mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Noticed the hanging sentence right after I posted it and edited it before the buffer elapsed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've been wondering if the human 'spirit' has been split among their ghost and Astral 'world' and presumably some others. </div> </div> </div>Going off of the notion that Mummy's fivefold soul overlaps pretty extensively with the Subtle Arcana, the Spirit Arcanum corresponds to the &quot;heart&quot; that serves as the seat of emotion and the capacity of things for emotional resonance \u2014 it could be that the Subtle Arcana being bound together to make a soul prevents the human heart from manifesting as a separate spiritual entity, in contrast to the shadow, which is close to Twilight as part of its nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T15:28:40-08:00","id":1030278,"title":"","content":"I just think of it as turning into something similar to the strix. Death can effectively turn you into the ghost realm, so Shadow Flesh turns you into a pseudo-strix shadow realm.<br /> <br /> <br /> Death is an Arcana of transformation, which also plays a part. Forces and Prime are the Arcana of energy. So, the two of them should acomplish different things based on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T18:47:28-08:00","id":1030377,"title":"","content":"My 'justification' of Shadow Flesh is that the mage is actually weakening the target so much that it almost destroys it entirely and maintains this half state, turning the target into it's shadow. And the 4th dot is capable of this feat but it should be Unraveling not a Perfecting spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T01:10:16-08:00","id":1030467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027564-turning-into-living-flame-how-to-do-this-in-second-edition?p=1030377#post1030377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My 'justification' of Shadow Flesh is that the mage is actually weakening the target so much that it almost destroys it entirely and maintains this half state, turning the target into it's shadow. And the 4th dot is capable of this feat but it should be Unraveling not a Perfecting spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a patterning (transformation) spell. Given, that the shadow of the subject is actually part of it's metaphysical self instead of just a physical phenomenon caused by a light source and the shape of the subjects body, you could say, that you transform this part of the subjects form to hold it's mind and soul, while at the same time temporarily destroying the other part (body). Both practices are well under the purview of Death. So it's probably patterning and unraveling, while I think the patterning part is more important, since just destroying the body wouldn't have the same effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}